  "title": "epan: Abort on start idle count if WIRESHARK_ABORT_ON_TOO_MANY_ITEMS",
  "description": "The start idle count is similar to adding too many items to the tree,\nso if we're aborting on too many items (e.g., during fuzz testing),\nalso abort on the start idle count. Because the start idle count\nboundary is lower (by default), we can hit it and throw a DissectorError\nin 4.6 and later and never hit the too many items error that was hit\nin 4.4 and earlier.\n\nPing #21263\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
